0..77 Comment "// The weakest-precondition observation of state: a handler of state into the"
78..155 Comment "// predicate transformers `((A, S) => Type, S) => Type`, from a postcondition"
156..222 Comment "// on the answer and the final state, and an initial state, to the"
223..297 Comment "// precondition the program needs there (Maillard et al., \"Dijkstra Monads"
298..374 Comment "// for All\", ICFP 2019, § 3.4, uncurried, with propositions read as types)."
375..441 Comment "// A scope answers its carrier, so the program it runs ends in the"
442..520 Comment "// transformers\' unit at its answer, and each clause is its operation\'s image:"
521..596 Comment "// a read hands the initial state to what runs after, and a store runs what"
597..673 Comment "// follows from the stored value. The scope is checked as a model of state\'s"
674..751 Comment "// laws, so the observation identifies what the laws identify, and is a monad"
752..830 Comment "// morphism from programs over state (§ 4.4 derives it from the state algebra"
831..908 Comment "// at the answer `S => Type`). The normaliser runs no scope yet (#2754), so a"
909..983 Comment "// precondition is computed through the fold `tree-state-wp.gandr` writes."
985..1000 Comment "// `StateLaws`."
